  "FiniteJetOver.chartEquiv": {
    "html": "<div class=\"lean-knowl-head\"><span class=\"lean-decl-kind\">def</span> <code>FiniteJetOver.chartEquiv</code></div><div class=\"lean-doc\"><p><strong>[FJP] Proposition 3.1</strong> over a general base: the chart is the square-zero disc<br>algebra, <code>𝒪_𝓐({|W| ≤ |ϖ|}) ≅ K⟨X⟩[Q]/(Q²) = 𝓑</code>, as topological rings.</p></div><pre class=\"lean-source\"><code class=\"language-lean\">def chartEquiv (ϖ : Uniformizer K) : presheafValue (chartDatum K ϖ) ≃+* JetB K</code></pre><div class=\"lean-source-meta\">projects/AdicSpaces/Adic spaces/FJP/Over/Chart.lean:1431–1431 · commit b007a4f3d422</div>",
    "href": "./lean/AdicSpaces/declarations/FiniteJetOver.chartEquiv.html"
  },
  "FiniteJetOver.chartEquiv_canonicalMap_W": {
    "html": "<div class=\"lean-knowl-head\"><span class=\"lean-decl-kind\">theorem</span> <code>FiniteJetOver.chartEquiv_canonicalMap_W</code></div><div class=\"lean-doc\"><p>The chart equivalence is the canonical one of [FJP] Prop 3.1 (&quot;<code>W ↦ ϖX</code>, <code>Q ↦ Q</code>&quot;):<br>it sends <code>ρ(W)</code> to <code>ϖ·jB(W)</code> (the <code>ϖ</code>-scaled disc variable) and <code>ρ(Q)</code> to the square-zero<br>generator <code>ε</code>.</p></div><pre class=\"lean-source\"><code class=\"language-lean\">theorem chartEquiv_canonicalMap_W (ϖ : Uniformizer K) :\n    chartEquiv K ϖ ((chartDatum K ϖ).canonicalMap (Wa K)) = piB ϖ * jB K (Wa K) ∧\n    chartEquiv K ϖ ((chartDatum K ϖ).canonicalMap (Qa K)) = TrivSqZeroExt.inr 1</code></pre><div class=\"lean-source-meta\">projects/AdicSpaces/Adic spaces/FJP/Over/Chart.lean:1446–1448 · commit b007a4f3d422</div>",
    "href": "./lean/AdicSpaces/declarations/FiniteJetOver.chartEquiv_canonicalMap_W.html"
  },
